<!--
  =====================================================================
  library/apps/services/soap/library.xml

  Book-oriented XML catalog of the online library.

  Source of truth:
      data/schema.sql   (structure, PostgreSQL schema "library")
      data/seed.sql     (initial data)

  Design notes
  * The document is BOOK-ORIENTED: <book> is the aggregate root and every
    piece of information hangs from the book it belongs to. Consumers of
    the SOAP service can therefore return a single <book> element as a
    complete, self-contained payload without extra joins.

  * The relational model is flattened into the book element following the
    functional dependencies documented in data/schema.sql:

      ISBN -> title, publicationYear, price, stock, format, category
          => plain child elements / attributes of <book>

      book ->> author            (multivalued dependency)
      book ->> genre             (multivalued dependency)
      book ->> image             (multivalued dependency)
      book ->> (concept, definition)
          => repeating wrapper elements <authors>, <genres>, <images>,
             <concepts>, so no MVD is ever collapsed into a delimited
             string.

  * (book, concept) -> definition is a dependency over the composite key:
    the same concept may carry a different definition in a different
    book, so <definition> lives inside <concept>, never inside the
    catalog entry.

  * Catalog entities (format, category, genre, author, concept) keep
    their database id in a "ref" attribute so the XML can be mapped back
    to the normalized tables without matching by name.

  * Element and attribute names are in English. Data values are
    reproduced verbatim as stored in the database.
  =====================================================================
-->
